{"blocks":[["CursorAI/Settings/Models/","source-block-2774","Provider: DeepSeek",["Cursor – Models","Model Information Table","DeepSeek/Model/r1"]],["CursorAI/Settings/Models/","source-block-2802","Premium: ✅ (Coming soon)",["Cursor – Models","Model Information Table","DeepSeek/Model/r1"]],["CursorAI/Settings/Models/","source-block-2838","Agent: ❌ (Coming soon)",["Cursor – Models","Model Information Table","DeepSeek/Model/r1"]],["CursorAI/Settings/Models/","source-block-2872","Pricing: $0.04",["Cursor – Models","Model Information Table","DeepSeek/Model/r1"]],["CursorAI/Settings/Models/","source-block-2896","Note: —",["Cursor – Models","Model Information Table","DeepSeek/Model/r1"]],["CursorAI/Sites/cursor.directory/","source-block-0","cursor.directory",[]],["CursorAI/Sites/cursor.directory/mcp/","source-block-0","Find MCP servers at cursor.directory",[]],["CursorAI/Status%20Page/","source-block-0","https://status.cursor.com/",[]],["CursorAI/Subagent/","source-block-0","Subagents – Cursor Docs",[]],["CursorAI/Subagent/","source-block-67","CursorAI's implementation of AI/Agent/Subagent: specialized agents with their own context, for task-specific work. Three ship built in — explore for codebase search, bash for shell commands, and browser for browser automation over MCP.",["Subagents – Cursor Docs"]],["CursorAI/Subagent/","source-block-322","Custom definitions are Markdown files in an agents/ directory and can be packaged in a CursorAI/Plugin, per the plugins reference.",["Subagents – Cursor Docs"]],["CursorAI/Subagent/","source-block-507","The declarable frontmatter surface is much smaller than Claude/Code/Subagent's, so a Claude agent definition loses fields on the way across.",["Subagents – Cursor Docs"]],["CursorAI/Subagent/","source-block-655","Support for a component is not the same as plugin parity: the plugins reference says these bundles work in the Cursor IDE and makes no equivalent claim for CursorAI/CLI. Test agents in the CLI independently of an IDE install.",["Subagents – Cursor Docs"]],["CursorAI/Technique/Composer/Keep%20it%20Short/","source-block-0","Quote",[]],["CursorAI/Technique/Composer/Keep%20it%20Short/","source-block-8","CursorAI/Technique/Frontload Design",["Quote"]],["CursorAI/Technique/Composer/Keep%20it%20Short/","source-block-313","CursorAI/Technique/Composer/Git Commit Frequently",["Quote"]],["CursorAI/Technique/Composer/Keep%20it%20Short/","source-block-471","Source",[]],["CursorAI/Technique/Composer/Single%20Purpose/","source-block-98","eric zakariasson on X: \"single purpose composers that's one of the patterns i apply to get the most out of @cursor_ai. i often see people using really long composers mixing up unrelated changes, causing the models to get confused. by creating new composers (cmd + n) you start fresh with a clean slate\" / X TwitX/ericzakariasson",[]],["CursorAI/Technique/Logseq/Summarize%20Meetings/","source-block-16","Use CursorAI and Logseq to summarize meetings",[]],["CursorAI/Technique/Logseq/Summarize%20Meetings/","source-block-67","Download a transcript into a vtt file, rename it to .txt",["Use CursorAI and Logseq to summarize meetings"]],["CursorAI/Technique/Logseq/Summarize%20Meetings/","source-block-133","put it in assets folder",["Use CursorAI and Logseq to summarize meetings"]],["CursorAI/Technique/Logseq/Summarize%20Meetings/","source-block-160","use cursor AI to refactor it into a script",["Use CursorAI and Logseq to summarize meetings"]],["CursorAI/Technique/Logseq/Summarize%20Meetings/","source-block-206","sample prompt",["Use CursorAI and Logseq to summarize meetings","use cursor AI to refactor it into a script"]],["CursorAI/Technique/Logseq/Summarize%20Meetings/","source-block-224","Can you please refactor @link-to-transcript-txt-file so it reads like a script",["Use CursorAI and Logseq to summarize meetings","use cursor AI to refactor it into a script","sample prompt"]],["CursorAI/Technique/Project%20Rules/GitHub%20Gist%20Auto-Updater/","source-block-0","GitHub/Gi